    fix: resolve INT-CI-033 CI test-count drift
    
    AGENTS.md documented 239 suites / 2021 tests while the live suite reports
    242 suites / 2027 tests. The docs literal was never re-synced after the
    recovered wave merged new test files, so every CI run since 10:38Z failed
    at the "Assert AGENTS.md test counts match live suite" step only
    (40859204988, 40891020172, 40897321388 — job "test", step failure; product
    test/build steps were green).
    
    Counts synced through the sanctioned single extraction path, never hand-typed:
    
      bash scripts/sync-agents-md-counts.sh /tmp/vitest-INT-CI-033.out
      -> AGENTS.md synced to live suite: 242 suites, 2027 tests
      bash scripts/sync-agents-md-counts.sh --check /tmp/vitest-INT-CI-033.out
      -> AGENTS.md test counts match live suite (242 suites, 2027 tests)
    
    Evidence: local full suite in this worktree at origin/main 327805b8
    (CI=true vm run, 77s) -> Test Files 242 passed (242), Tests 2027 passed
    (2027), zero failures; identical to the live CI totals (242/2027) in runs
    40860007523, 40862537937, 40889751826, 40891020172, 40897321388. The board
    row's 2028 was a pre-merge reading (run 40859204988 still had 241/2026).
    
    Row AC-3 (make the verifier tolerant: range or dynamic baseline) is
    DECLINED deliberately: scripts/sync-agents-md-counts.sh is not brittle — it
    reported the exact live pair and the drift is real. Loosening the equality
    would let tests disappear without a red, which is the failure class the gate
    was created for after four earlier hand-typed drifts (GAP-006, GAP-008,
    GAP-012, CI-005). Only the docs literals change; no test logic is touched.
    
    Docs-only change; node scripts/docs-check.js OK (README + 49 docs files).
    
    Addresses INT-CI-033.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
